# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artefacts
#
# Nothing here is authored. Datasets are downloaded, weights and training
# runs are produced by scripts/, and everything under results/ is
# regenerated on demand. The repository tracks the code that makes them and
# the documentation that interprets them.
#
# These are directory-wide rules on purpose. An earlier version listed each
# output directory by name, which meant every new script needed a matching
# .gitignore entry and silently did not get one - ten directories were
# untracked and unignored before this was fixed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Everything produced under results/, except the README that says what
# lands where and which script produced it.
results/*
!results/README.md

# Ultralytics training runs.
runs/

# Datasets: downloaded or converted, never authored. The per-dataset
# data.yaml is the exception - it is configuration, it is small, and the
# conversion scripts need it.
raw_data/
dataset/*
!dataset/*/
dataset/*/*
!dataset/*/data.yaml

# Model weights and exported graphs.
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine

# Archives.
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo

venv/
.venv/

# Ultralytics label caches.
*.cache

# Claude Code working directories, including Git worktrees.
.claude/

.vscode/
.idea/

Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
